{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to understand the pattern in which the sequence is generated. The sequence is constructed by listing a certain number of integers and then skipping a certain number of integers, with the number of integers listed and skipped increasing step by step.\n\nThe sequence is generated as follows:\n- On the 1st iteration, list 4 and skip 1.\n- On the 2nd iteration, list 5 and skip 2.\n- On the 3rd iteration, list 6 and skip 3.\n- On the \\( n \\)-th iteration, list \\( n + 3 \\) and skip \\( n \\).\n\nThe total number of integers listed and skipped up to the \\( n \\)-th iteration is:\n\\[ 4 + 5 + 6 + \\cdots + (n+3) + (1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + n) \\]\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) positive integers is \\( \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\). So, the total number of integers listed and skipped up to the \\( n \\)-th iteration is:\n\\[ \\sum_{k=4}^{n+3} k + \\sum_{k=1}^{n} k = \\frac{(n+3)(n+4)}{2} - 6 + \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{(n+3)(n+4) + n(n+1) - 12}{2} = \\frac{n^2 + 7n + 12 + n^2 + n - 12}{2} = \\frac{2n^2 + 8n}{2} = n^2 + 4n \\]\n\n","prefix_end":1028,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,3535,279,5383,304,892,279,8500,374,7907,13,576,8500,374,20346,553,14838,264,3654,1372,315,25780,323,1221,42659,264,3654,1372,315,25780,11,448,279,1372,315,25780,10007,323,35157,7703,3019,553,3019,382,785,8500,374,7907,438,11017,510,12,1913,279,220,16,267,19569,11,1140,220,19,323,10706,220,16,624,12,1913,279,220,17,303,19569,11,1140,220,20,323,10706,220,17,624,12,1913,279,220,18,6498,19569,11,1140,220,21,323,10706,220,18,624,12,1913,279,17767,308,1124,7287,339,19569,11,1140,17767,308,488,220,18,1124,8,323,10706,17767,308,1124,3593,785,2790,1372,315,25780,10007,323,35157,705,311,279,17767,308,1124,7287,339,19569,374,510,78045,220,19,488,220,20,488,220,21,488,1124,4385,2412,